  "summary": "Cooling-water pumps circulate large volumes of water through heat exchangers, condensers and process coolers at moderate head. A horizontally split-case, double-suction pump is a common choice: high flow with low NPSH required, balanced axial thrust, long bearing life with bearings at both ends of the shaft, and the whole rotor can be lifted out after removing the upper casing half without disturbing the piping or motor. Typical installations run duty/standby pumps with check and isolation valves on each.",
  "classification": {
    "family": "Rotodynamic (centrifugal), radial flow",
    "configuration": "Horizontal, axially split, double suction, between bearings",
    "api_610_type": "BB1",
    "application": "Open/closed cooling water circuits, condenser cooling, HVAC chilled/condenser water"
  },
  "model_configuration": {
    "driver": "Foot-mounted TEFC motor with flexible spacer coupling",
    "valves": "Suction isolation, discharge non-return and isolation",
    "water_quality_note": "Seawater/raw water needs material selection (bronze, duplex) and strainers upstream."
  },
